Random exact stress
  samples=80
  positive Bonferroni3 tails=32
  max tail:  0.102699587 (231661/2255715) case= ([0, 11, 14], [18, 22, 25, 27, 28, 31], Fraction(231661, 2255715), {0: Fraction(0, 1), 1: Fraction(0, 1), 2: Fraction(0, 1), 3: Fraction(0, 1), 4: Fraction(2094247, 22557150), 5: Fraction(797, 80850), 6: Fraction(0, 1)}, 1)
  max p0 among positive-tail cases:  0.461262547 (48481/105105) case= ([0, 1, 5, 8, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14], [16, 22, 24, 32], Fraction(47, 84084), {0: Fraction(0, 1), 1: Fraction(0, 1), 2: Fraction(1, 924), 3: Fraction(-1, 728), 4: Fraction(1, 1176), 5: Fraction(0, 1), 6: Fraction(0, 1)}, 1)

Proof correction
  The Newton expansion is exact, but the high-tail sign is a depth
  parity inequality, not a consequence of Venn containment alone.
  A viable proof target is:
    (positive even-depth high packets) <= (negative odd-depth high packets) + cap slack,
  with deep-missing rows routed to an easy small-p0/decorrelation bound.

Tournament Analysis
  vertices: proof carriers, not runners
  observable: exactness + survived falsification + proof usefulness + label retention
  score_hist={0: 1, 1: 1, 2: 1, 3: 1, 4: 1, 5: 1}
  directed_3cycles=0
  Hamiltonian path=pointwise_depth_formula > depth_parity_tail_inequality > doublet_plus_triple_cap > bonferroni3_unconditional > raw_venn_containment > raw_runner_vertices
